ors:\n\n12/25A \u00d7 75 = 800 \u00d7 75 + 4/75A \u00d7 75\n\n12 \u00d7 3A = 60000 + 4A\n\n36A = 60000 + 4A\n\n32A = 60000\n\nA = 60000 / 32 = 1875. Same result. So confirms the same answer.\n\nTherefore, the original inventory of Warehouse A was 1875 tons.", "deepseek_solution": "Let \\( A \\) be the original inventory of Warehouse A in tons. The problem states the following steps:\n\n1. **Initial Inventories:**\n   - Warehouse A: \\( A \\) tons\n   - Warehouse B: \\( 1200 \\) tons\n\n2. **Goods Transported Out:**\n   - From A: \\( \\frac{7}{15}A \\) removed. Remaining in A: \\( A - \\frac{7}{15}A = \\frac{8}{15}A \\).\n   - From B: \\( \\frac{1}{3} \\times 1200 = 400 \\) tons removed. Remaining in B: \\( 1200 - 400 = 800 \\) tons.\n\n3. **10% Transfer from A to B:**\n   - 10% of remaining in A: \\( 0.1 \\times \\frac{8}{15}A = \\frac{4}{75}A \\).\n   - New inventory in A: \\( \\frac{8}{15}A - \\frac{4}{75}A \\).\n   - New inventory in B: \\( 800 + \\frac{4}{75}A \\).\n\n4. **Equate Final Inventories:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{8}{15}A - \\frac{4}{75}A = 800 + \\frac{4}{75}A\n   \\]\n   Simplify:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{40}{75}A - \\frac{4}{75}A = 800 + \\frac{4}{75}A \\implies \\frac{32}{75}A = 800 \\implies A = 800 \\times \\frac{75}{32} = 1875\n   \\]\n\n**Verification:**\n- After removing \\( \\frac{7}{15} \\times 1875 = 875 \\) tons, A has \\( 1000 \\) tons.\n- B has \\( 800 \\) tons after removal.\n- Transfer 10% of 1000 tons (\\( 100 \\) tons) from A to B:\n  - A: \\( 900 \\) tons, B: \\( 900 \\) tons.\n\n**Answer:** Warehouse A originally had \\(\\boxed{1875}\\) tons of inventory.", "ground_truth_solution": "Let \\( x \\) be the original amount of goods in the \\( \\text{\u7532} \\) warehouse.\n\n1. After moving \\( \\frac{7}{15} \\) of the goods from the \\( \\text{\u7532} \\) warehouse, the remaining goods are:\n   \\[\n   x \\times \\left(1 - \\frac{7}{15}\\right) = x \\times \\frac{8}{15}\n   \\]\n\n2. The \\( \\text{\u4e59} \\) warehouse originally had 1200 units