at's correct.\n\nSo, summarizing:\n\nT\u2085 = 16x\u2075 -20x\u00b3 +5x\n\nSum T\u2080 + T\u2081 + T\u2082 + T\u2083 =4x\u00b3 +2x\u00b2 -2x\n\nI think that's all. Let me just check if the coefficients for T\u2085 are correct. Let's re-derive T\u2084 and T\u2085 once again.\n\nStarting from T\u2080=1, T\u2081=x\n\nT\u2082 =2x*T\u2081 -T\u2080=2x*x -1=2x\u00b2 -1\n\nT\u2083=2x*T\u2082 -T\u2081=2x*(2x\u00b2 -1) -x=4x\u00b3 -2x -x=4x\u00b3 -3x\n\nT\u2084=2x*T\u2083 -T\u2082=2x*(4x\u00b3 -3x) - (2x\u00b2 -1)=8x\u2074 -6x\u00b2 -2x\u00b2 +1=8x\u2074 -8x\u00b2 +1\n\nT\u2085=2x*T\u2084 -T\u2083=2x*(8x\u2074 -8x\u00b2 +1) - (4x\u00b3 -3x)=16x\u2075 -16x\u00b3 +2x -4x\u00b3 +3x=16x\u2075 -20x\u00b3 +5x\n\nYes, that's correct. So T\u2085 is indeed 16x\u2075 -20x\u00b3 +5x.\n\nAnd the sum T\u2080+T\u2081+T\u2082+T\u2083 is 4x\u00b3 +2x\u00b2 -2x. I think that's all. I don't see any mistakes here.", "deepseek_solution": "To solve for \\( T_5 \\) and the sum \\( T_0 + T_1 + T_2 + T_3 \\), we use the recurrence relation \\( T_{k+1} = 2xT_k - T_{k-1} \\) with initial terms \\( T_0 = 1 \\) and \\( T_1 = x \\).\n\n**Calculating \\( T_2 \\) to \\( T_5 \\):**\n- \\( T_2 = 2xT_1 - T_0 = 2x(x) - 1 = 2x^2 - 1 \\)\n- \\( T_3 = 2xT_2 - T_1 = 2x(2x^2 - 1) - x = 4x^3 - 3x \\)\n- \\( T_4 = 2xT_3 - T_2 = 2x(4x^3 - 3x) - (2x^2 - 1) = 8x^4 - 8x^2 + 1 \\)\n- \\( T_5 = 2xT_4 - T_3 = 2x(8x^4 - 8x^2 + 1) - (4x^3 - 3x) = 16x^5 - 20x^3 + 5x \\)\n\n**Summing \\( T_0 + T_1 + T_2 + T_3 \\):**\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nT_0 + T_1 + T_2 + T_3 &= 1 + x + (2x^2 - 1) + (4x^3 - 3x) \\\\\n&= (1 - 1) + (x - 3x) + 2x^2 + 4x^3 \\\\\n&= 4x^3 + 2x^2 - 2x\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n**Final Results:**\n- \\( T_5 = \\boxed{16x^5 - 20x^3 + 5x} \\)\n- \\( T_0 + T_1 + T_2 + T_3 = \\boxed{4x^3 + 2x^2 - 2x} \\)", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. First, note the initial conditions and recursive relation for the Chebyshev polynomials of the first kind:\n   \\[\n   T_0 = 1, \\quad T_1 = x, \\quad \\text{and} \\quad T_{k+1} = 2x T_k - T_{k-1} \\quad \\text{for} \\quad k \\in \\mathbb{N}.\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(T_2\\) using the given recursion:\n   \\[\n   T_2 = 2x T_1 - T_0 = 2x \\cdot x - 1 = 2x^2 - 1.\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(T_3\\) using the recursion:\n   \\[\n   T_3 = 2x T_2 - T_1 = 2x (2x^2 - 1) - x = 4x^3 - 2x - x = 4x^3 - 3x.\n   \\]\n\n4. Calculate \\(T_4\\) using the recursion:\n   \\[\n   T_4 = 2x T_3 - T_2 = 2x (4x^3 - 3x) - (2x^2 - 1) = 8x^4 - 6x^2 - 2x^2 + 1 = 8x^4 - 8x^2 + 1.\n   \\]\n\n5. Calculate \\(T_5\\) using the recursion:\n   \\[\n   T_5 = 2x T_4 - T_3 = 2x (8x^4 - 8x^2 + 1) - (4x^3 - 3x) = 16x^5 - 16x^3 + 2x - 4x^3 + 3x = 16x^5 - 20x^3 + 5x.\n   \\]\n\n6. Calculate the sum \\( T_0 + T_1 + T_2 + T_3 \\):\n   \\[\n   T_0 + T_1 + T_2 + T_3 = 1 + x + (2x^2 - 1) + (4x^3 - 3x).\n   \\]\n\n7. Simplify the sum step-by-step:\n   \\[\n   T_0 + T_1 + T_2 + T_3 = 1 + x + 2x^2 - 1 + 4x^3 - 3x.\n   \\]\n   Combine like terms:\n   \\[\n   1 - 1 + x - 3x + 2x^2 + 4x^3 = 4x^3 + 2x^2 - 2x.\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{T_5 = 16x^5 - 20x^3 + 5x, \\quad T_0 + T_1 + T_2 + T_3 = 4x^3 + 2x^2 - 2x.}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "In an isosceles triangle \\( ABC \\) with \\(\\angle B = \\arctan \\frac{8}{15}\\), a circle with radius 1 is inscribed in angle \\( C \\) and touches side \\( CB \\) at point \\( M \\) and cuts off a segment \\( KE \\) from the base. It is known that \\( MB = \\frac{15}{8} \\). Find the area of triangle \\( KMB \\), given that points \\( A, K, E, B \\) follow in the mentioned order along the base \\( AB \\).", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, let's try to tackle this geometry problem step by step. First, I need to understand the given information and visualize the problem. So, we have an isosceles triangle \\( ABC \\) with \\( \\angle B = \\arctan \\frac{8}{15} \\). There's a circle inscribed in angle \\( C \\) with radius 1, touching side \\( CB \\) at point \\( M \\), and cutting off